   $q$What is the effect of beginning sentences 14, 15 and 16 with "At six," "At seven," and "At eight"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They signal that each sentence is told by a different character.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-pov-shift"},{"text":"They move the story quickly through the morning in clear time order toward the exam.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They slow the story down to describe each hour in great detail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"},{"text":"They show that the events happened in a random order.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-time-order"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They move the story quickly through the morning in clear time order toward the exam.$q$, $q$The repeated time markers speed the story through three hours and lead straight to the test. Each sentence gets only a brief detail, so the pace is faster, not slower.$q$, 'draft', '60cc69e9-9e03-5e89-a4bc-92bc62f2dd71')
