   $q$Why does the narrator "almost laugh" in sentence 17?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator is nervous and laughs whenever a test begins.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The narrator remembers that Mr. Yamada is also a chemistry teacher.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-unstated-detail"},{"text":"The idea of a limiting reagent matches the morning, when the small oven limited how much bread they could bake.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The test question is so easy that the narrator finds it silly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The idea of a limiting reagent matches the morning, when the small oven limited how much bread they could bake.$q$, $q$Sentence 12 says the smaller oven forced them to bake in batches, which mirrors the idea of a limiting factor and ties the two plot lines together. The story never says the question was easy.$q$, 'draft', '60cc69e9-9e03-5e89-a4bc-92bc62f2dd71')
